Local modification to CMSIS-DSP v1.15.0: RMS instead of absmax pre-FFT scaling
in arm_mfcc_f32().

Origin is undocumented. The identical modification is present in both copies
that entered this repository on 2026-08-07 (fw/bom-stm32node/third_party and
the drony CubeIDE workspace on hermakam/drones-research), so it was applied by
hand to the downloaded v1.15.0 archive before either was committed.

What it changes: arm_mfcc_f32() conditions the input for the FFT by scaling it
to unit level and scaling the magnitude spectrum back afterwards. Upstream uses
the absolute maximum (guard: maxValue != 0.0f); this tree uses the RMS (guard:
rmsValue > 1e-6f). The scale-and-unscale pair is linear and cancels in exact
arithmetic, so this is not a change of definition - it changes float32 rounding,
and it changes behaviour for frames quieter than the guard, which upstream still
normalises and this version leaves alone.

Why it must not be lost: the deployed model (mlp_model_data_v6.h) was selected
against MFCC values produced by THIS code path. Reverting to upstream silently
perturbs every coefficient. When third_party/CMSIS-DSP is replaced by a CMake
FetchContent of v1.15.0, re-apply this patch (or re-baseline the detector on
hardware and record the new decision values).

Apply with: git apply patches/0001-mfcc-rms-normalisation.patch
Verify with: cmp against the v1.15.0 release archive; only this file may differ.

--- a/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_mfcc_f32.c
+++ b/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_mfcc_f32.c
@@ -81,12 +81,13 @@
   const float32_t *coefs=S->filterCoefs;
   arm_matrix_instance_f32 pDctMat;
 
-  /* Normalize */
-  arm_absmax_f32(pSrc,S->fftLen,&maxValue,&index);
+  /* RMS Normalize */
+  float32_t rmsValue;
+  arm_rms_f32(pSrc,S->fftLen,&rmsValue);
 
-  if (maxValue != 0.0f)
+  if (rmsValue > 1e-6f)
   {
-     arm_scale_f32(pSrc,1.0f/maxValue,pSrc,S->fftLen);
+     arm_scale_f32(pSrc,1.0f/rmsValue,pSrc,S->fftLen);
   }
 
   /* Multiply by window */
@@ -118,9 +119,9 @@
   pTmp[1]=0.0f;
 #endif
   arm_cmplx_mag_f32(pTmp,pSrc,S->fftLen);
-  if (maxValue != 0.0f)
+  if (rmsValue > 1e-6f)
   {
-     arm_scale_f32(pSrc,maxValue,pSrc,S->fftLen);
+     arm_scale_f32(pSrc,rmsValue,pSrc,S->fftLen);
   }
 
   /* Apply MEL filters */
